	'story_h' => 'Our story',
	'story_p1' => 'Hanna Weiss opened Enogu Supply on Calder Row in 2011 with a single plan chest and the specialist papers she could not find anywhere in town. As a working bookbinder and printmaker, she wanted an independent shop where artists could buy full cotton sheets from drawers rather than pre-cut pads, finding reliable, unbranded materials that perform consistently under ink and wash.',
	'story_p2' => 'Daily life at the counter follows an unhurried workshop routine. Tomás Ferreira slides open the wide plan chests to cut sheets to custom dimensions while customers wait, Amara Nwosu keeps water pots and testing strips ready so students can wet a brush before choosing, and Leo Marchetti spends Mondays packing orders flat between boards.',
